cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "execution-lab: a transparent execution-cost and market-impact laboratory"
abstract: >-
  A small, reproducible laboratory for asking whether a portfolio edge survives
  realistic transaction costs. It decomposes cost into half-spread, commission,
  square-root market impact, and timing risk; compares immediate, TWAP, VWAP, and
  POV schedules; and shows how strategy rankings change with order size, impact
  coefficient, and assets under management. The checked-in demo uses a synthetic
  ETF panel. The model is a teaching and engineering tool, not a live execution
  simulator, and it makes no tradable-alpha claim.
authors:
